> a(x: u32, y: u32, z: u32) = (x*y+z)*y
> b(x: u32, y: u32, z: u32) = x*y*y+z*y
> equiv a b
a and b are equal on the domain of a (proved by algebra: both sides expand to one polynomial in x, y, z mod 2^32)
> c(x: u32, y: u32, z: u32) = (x*y+z)*y
> d(x: u32, y: u32, z: u32) = x*y*y+z
> equiv c d
c and d differ at 65532 points of the sample, e.g. x=4294967295, y=0, z=2: 0 vs 2
